  <translations>
    <en>
      <description>Rain Bird 150-PGA is a professional solenoid valve with a 1 1/2″ connection for systems requiring higher flow. It can be installed inline or at an angle and is used to control zones in large gardens, parks and commercial landscapes. This version uses a 24 VAC solenoid. PGA series pressure reaches approximately 10.4 bar; required flow should be determined by hydraulic design.</description>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>b0</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>b00</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <marks>strong</marks>
          <text>150-PGA</text>
        </children>
        <children>
          <_key>b01</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text> — a 1″ diaphragm solenoid valve for automatic irrigation.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>h1</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>h10</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Purpose and operating principle</text>
        </children>
        <style>h2</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>p1</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>p10</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>The controller energises the solenoid, which operates the diaphragm and opens the water passage. When the signal stops, the valve closes automatically. The PGA series is a professional range with inline or angle installation, filtered pilot flow, slow closing and manual operation.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>h2</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>h20</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Construction and model-specific features</text>
        </children>
        <style>h2</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>p2</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>p20</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>The integrated flow-control handle adjusts delivery; internal manual operation simplifies service and slow closing helps reduce water-hammer risk. The PRS-D pressure-regulating module is optional, sold separately and not included.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>h3</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>h30</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Hydraulic and electrical specifications</text>
        </children>
        <style>h2</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>p3</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>p30</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <marks>strong</marks>
          <text>Size 1½″; operating pressure 1,04–10,4 bar; flow 30–100 GPM (6,81–22,70 m³/h); solenoid 24 VAC. Actual flow depends on pipe, filter and fitting losses as well as available pressure.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>h4</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>h40</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Installation, adjustment and maintenance</text>
        </children>
        <style>h2</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>p4</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>p40</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Connection: 1½″ female NPT thread. Before installation, confirm flow direction, operating pressure and thread standard. Fit the valve in an accessible valve box and flush the pipework before commissioning. During service, inspect the diaphragm, pilot filter, solenoid and seals. For flows below 2.27 m³/h, set the flow-control stem two full turns from fully open; below 1.14 m³/h, upstream filtration is recommended.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>l0</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>l00</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Check flow direction and stay within the permitted operating pressure.</text>
        </children>
        <level>1</level>
        <listItem>bullet</listItem>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>l1</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>l10</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Flush pipework before connection to keep sand and swarf out of the pilot circuit.</text>
        </children>
        <level>1</level>
        <listItem>bullet</listItem>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>l2</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>l20</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Leave access for future maintenance.</text>
